Z||000016||Cheever2||03-12-2001||12:53 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tigger:<BR><B>wondering what the guy was thinking at the time he filled the corners of his trunk with that stuff.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Pontoons?  Maybe he was gonna add a propeller PTO and go amphibious.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/swimw3.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/swimw2.jpg"> <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||Coconut||03-12-2001||04:10 PM||||Geez Hugh,<BR> Seemed like a pretty 'sticky' dillema if you ask me! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Sorry, I know,- VERY bad pun.<P>Kinda brings back a situation that occured  quite a few years back, that wasn't so funny when it happened, but sure makes everybody laugh at the dinner table now.<P>My mom needed to glue something together and didn't have anything so she asked me if I had any glue. I said "sure, I got some super glue in my desk". Mom had never used or even heard of super glue at the time, and she was having difficulty getting the cap off, so after a few hard tugs that didn't work, she got impatient and decided to use her TEETH to bite the cap off! Yeah, the lid came off, but since this superglue had a watery consistency, it glued her lips shut!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>Everything turned out okay, but my Dad swears that in the 40 some odd years that they've been married, that was the first time that he has had any peace! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">! He didn't have to listen to her chattering for a good half hour! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Cruisin' <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Coconut's_Signature_1.JPG"> ||||reg||12
Z||000018||rogergarrison||03-12-2001||08:25 PM||||another warning, if you spray it in a confined space remember it swells as it cures. A friend put in in a hollow part of his wood boat. Filled it up, went back to find it swelled out split and busted it all to pieces.  (NOT FUNNY) well ya, but me -not for him. lol||||reg||1
Z||000019||Jake_Dragon||03-12-2001||08:49 PM||||Well when I was young and in the navy we used the two-part foam to fill in pontoons.<BR>You basically have a 6-inch pipe 4 feet long. Basically just cap one end and add foam. Well as young people will do I did the something stupid, as the foam started to fill the pipe I capped the other end wanting to see the air pressure push off the cap. Wrong end came off and blasted the back door of our shop. That was a bad time to be E3. Can you say EMI? It took 2 days to strip the door and paint it.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">   <BR> <IMG SRC="http://home1.gte.net/rebel33/fiero.jpg"> ||||reg||8
Z||000020||hugh||03-13-2001||07:25 AM||||Now that I'm thinking of it,you can also be an artist with it.My brother had some left in a can and didn't want to waste it so he wrote his name in the dirt,let it cure and now has it hanging on the wall in our office.If you ever saw our office you would know it fits right in.We clean the floor with a shovel and broom,not a vacuum.||||reg||1
